<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="header">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header-tag">Strategic Intelligence Briefing</div>
    <h1>Biomedical Research Landscape 2024–2026</h1>
    <p class="header-subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of 4,886 biomedical research abstracts indexed in PubMed from January 2024 through March 2026 — examining temporal publication patterns, geographic contributions, dominant research topics, and open-access adoption.</p>
    <div class="header-meta">
      <span>📅 Reporting period: Jan 2024 – Mar 2026</span>
      <span>📊 Source: PubMed / NCBI</span>
      <span>🎯 Audience: Research Policy Analysts &amp; Funding Strategists</span>
      <span>📅 Report generated: April 2026</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- KPI ROW -->
<div class="container">
  <div class="kpi-grid" style="margin-top:40px;">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Publications</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">4,886</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Across 3 calendar years (2024–2026)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Open Access Rate</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">65.1%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">74.1% in 2025 <span class="kpi-badge">+10pp</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Authors / Article</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">6</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Consistent across all years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Top 10 Countries Share</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">51.2%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">China leads at 22.1% of total output</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Top MeSH Topic</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">COVID-19</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">43 tagged publications (declining trend)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Open Access (2026 YTD)</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">53.8%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Depressed by indexing lag (recent articles)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 1: Publication Volume & Temporal Distribution -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">01</span>
      <h2>Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Data context note:</strong> ~80% of records (3,924) are from 2024, reflecting real-world PubMed indexing lag — older publications accumulate more complete indexed entries over time. 2025 and early 2026 figures are meaningfully underrepresented and should be interpreted as lower bounds, not absolute output. Raw counts should not be compared across years without normalization.
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Annual Publication Distribution</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="annualChart" height="220"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Monthly Volume — 2024 (known months only)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="monthly2024Chart" height="220"></canvas>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Note: 575 records from 2024 have unknown month and are excluded from this view. Jan-2024 spike reflects bulk-indexing of prior-period records entering PubMed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">Monthly Publication Trend — Full Period (Jan 2024 – Mar 2026, known months)</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="fullTrendChart" height="180"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Unknown-month records excluded (754 total: 575 in 2024, 179 in 2025). 2025–2026 counts will grow as indexing catches up.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Key pattern:</strong> The January 2024 spike (1,665 publications with known months) reflects bulk retroactive indexing. Monthly counts from mid-2024 onward stabilize at 30–100 per month for dated records. The 2025 December surge (94 publications) and the 2026 Q1 ramp (Jan: 51, Feb: 76, Mar: 98) indicate genuine publication acceleration in early 2026.
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Publications by Year — Breakdown</div>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Count</th><th>Share</th><th>OA Rate</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>2024</td><td>3,924</td><td>80.3%</td><td>64.1%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2025</td><td>737</td><td>15.1%</td><td>74.1%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026 (Jan–Mar)</td><td>225</td><td>4.6%</td><td>53.8%</td></tr>
            <tr style="font-weight:700;background:#f5f8fd;"><td>Total</td><td>4,886</td><td>100%</td><td>65.1%</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">2025–2026 Monthly Trend (detailed)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="recent2526Chart" height="220"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 2: Geographic Landscape -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">02</span>
      <h2>Geographic Landscape of Biomedical Research</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Top 15 Countries by Publication Count (normalized)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="countryChart" height="360"></canvas>
        </div>
        <p class="note">USA counts consolidated (USA + United States). China consolidated (China + PR China + People's Republic of China + P R China). "Unknown" affiliation excluded.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Country Share of Total Output</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="countryPieChart" height="260"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="insight-box" style="margin-top:16px;">
          <strong>Geographic concentration:</strong> The top 10 countries account for 51.2% of all publications. China alone contributes 22.1%, followed by the USA at 11.0%. The top 3 (China, USA, India) represent 38% of indexed output.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">Top 5 Countries Over Time — Year-by-Year Comparison</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="countryTrendChart" height="200"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Raw counts shown. 2025 and 2026 are subject to indexing lag — China and USA maintain dominance across all years.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">Country Rankings Detail</div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Country</th><th>Publications</th><th>Share</th><th>Median Authors</th><th>2024</th><th>2025</th><th>2026</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td>China</td><td>1,082</td><td>22.1%</td><td>7</td><td>935</td><td>101</td><td>46</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td>USA</td><td>539</td><td>11.0%</td><td>6</td><td>443</td><td>74</td><td>22</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td>India</td><td>196</td><td>4.0%</td><td>5</td><td>129</td><td>59</td><td>8</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td>Japan</td><td>137</td><td>2.8%</td><td>6</td><td>113</td><td>18</td><td>6</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td>Canada</td><td>107</td><td>2.2%</td><td>5</td><td>89</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>6</td><td>Iran</td><td>107</td><td>2.2%</td><td>5</td><td>—</td><td>27</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>7</td><td>Germany</td><td>98</td><td>2.0%</td><td>6</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>8</td><td>Italy</td><td>89</td><td>1.8%</td><td>8</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>9</td><td>UK</td><td>78</td><td>1.6%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10</td><td>Republic of Korea</td><td>68</td><td>1.4%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">India's 2025 share (59 of 196 total = 30%) indicates disproportionately strong recent growth, potentially reflecting improved PubMed indexing coverage of Indian journals.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Strategic signal:</strong> India's 2025 representation (59 publications vs. 129 in 2024) suggests its relative share of the 2025 cohort (~8%) is nearly double its 2024 share (~3.3%), hinting at accelerating research output or indexing improvements. Iran similarly shows notable 2025 presence (27 publications).
